    "summary": "19‑min Playing In The Band + soaring third‑set jams make this a classic",
    "blurb": "The show features an epic 19‑minute “Playing In The Band” and a fire‑filled third set highlighted by “Truckin' > Nobody's Fault But Mine Jam > Other One”, “Eyes Of The World” and “Stella Blue”. Jerry’s raspy voice battles a cold but his guitar remains fiery, while Keith’s keyboards and Phil’s bass drive the improvisations. The Miller soundboard capture is pristine, delivering crystal‑clear balance throughout.",
    "review": "May 20, 1973 at UCSB captured one of the band’s most exhilarating late‑spring outings. A tight first set builds momentum into a jaw‑dropping 19‑minute “Playing In The Band” that showcases Jerry’s razor‑sharp leads and Phil’s emotive, fired‑up bass work. The second set lifts off with bright moments like “Here Comes Sunshine”, “Row Jimmy” and the ever‑playful “Bertha/China Cat Sunflower > I Know You Rider”. The third set is where the night truly soars: a seamless “Truckin' > Nobody's Fault But Mine Jam > The Other One” cascade, followed by a soaring “Eyes Of The World”, tender “Stella Blue” and an exuberant “Sugar Magnolia”. Across all five soundboard sources the band sounds locked in; Keith’s organ/piano is “on his game”, Donna’s harmonies are angelic, and Bill Kreutzmann provides booming, driving drums that propel each jam. Even though Jerry’s voice bears a cold‑induced rasp, reviewers note it adds an oddly sweet edge to his vocals. The Miller SBD (gd1973-05-20.sbd.miller.86905.sbeok.flac16) stands out as the cleanest, most balanced source, preserving every nuance of this high‑octane performance.",
